eason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"Originally reported by: **BitBucket: [carlio](http://bitbucket.org/carlio), GitHub: @carlio?**\n\n---\n\nA `dangerous-default-value` warning evaluates the value of the argument it is describing. If this is not empty, this can result in a long error message with unnecessary information.\n\nSpecifically for Landscape, if the default value is `os.environ`, then your environ including passwords gets dumped into your webUI! Obviously that's a bit of a special use case, however I feel like just the type of the argument would be sufficient.\n\nYou can reproduce this by running pylint on:\n\n```\nimport os\n\ndef do_a_thing(x=os.environ):\n    return len(x)\n```\n\nIf you agree that changing the message to return the type of the argument rather than the contents, I will happily create that PR myself.\n\n---\n- Bitbucket: https://bitbucket.org/logilab/pylint/issue/282\n","closed_by":{"login":"pylint-bot","id":16198247,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MTk4MjQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16198247?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/pylint-bot","html_url":"https://github.com/pylint-bot","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pylint-bot/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pylint-bot/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pylint-bot/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pylint-bot/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pylint-bot/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pylint-bot/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pylint-bot/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pylint-bot/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pylint-bot/received_events","type":"User","user_view_ty